# WATEEN (وَتِين) — AI PAIR PROGRAMMING CHARTER & CONSTITUTION

**Version**: 5.0 (B2B2C + WBS Edition)
**Updated**: March 1, 2026
**Target**: All AI Assistants, Language Models, and Copilots operating in this workspace.
**Source of Truth**: `AGENTS.md` (full contract) + `docs/AGILE_BACKLOG_WBS.md` (roadmap)

---

## STRICT DIRECTIVES: AVOID HALLUCINATION AND FATAL ERRORS

As an AI Agent working on Wateen, you are legally and technically constrained by the following core directives. **Do not hallucinate features, do not revert to P2P logic, and do not invent libraries outside the allowed stack.**

## 1. The B2B2C Architecture Mandate
Wateen is **NOT** a Peer-to-Peer (P2P) freelance marketplace. It is a strictly compliant B2B2C Aggregator.
- **NEVER** write code where a Nurse registers independently without an associated `AGENCY_PROFILE`.
- **NEVER** write code where Wateen pays a Nurse directly. Financials (`agency_payout`) are settled to the Agency's wallet.
- **ALWAYS** ensure `agency_id` is central to `NURSE_PROFILE`, `VISIT`, and `TRANSACTION` data boundaries.
- **ROUTING**: Patient visits are routed to the **AGENCY** based on `coverage_polygon` (PostGIS), not directly to the nearest Nurse.

## 2. Authorized Tech Stack (NO EXCEPTIONS)
You may only use the following technologies. Do not suggest or install alternatives unless explicitly instructed by the Solo Dev.

### Backend (Python/Django)
- Python 3.11+
- Django 5.x
- Django REST Framework (DRF)
- PostgreSQL with **PostGIS** extension (Spatial queries are mandatory)
- Redis & Django Channels (WebSockets for dispatching)
- Celery (Background tasks for routing timeouts and escrow calculations)

### Frontend (Next.js / React)
- TypeScript 5.x
- Next.js 14 (App Router exclusively)
- Tailwind CSS (v3/v4 depending on configuration)
- **OpenStreetMap stack ONLY**: react-leaflet, leaflet-geoman, Nominatim, OSRM/ORS
- **NO Google Maps, NO Mapbox** — banned for cost and vendor lock-in
- React Admin (Agency SaaS B2B Dashboard)
- next-intl (Arabic/English i18n)

### Payments
- Stripe Connect (Destination Charges, manual capture for escrow)

## 3. Database Modifications Rules
- Never use simple Float/Decimal for Locations. **ALWAYS** use `django.contrib.gis.db.models.PointField` or `PolygonField`.
- Migrations must never drop core user data without a safe fallback/idempotency script.
- Ensure `on_delete=CASCADE` is used safely; deleting an Agency MUST delete its Nurses to prevent orphaned entities violating MoH compliance.
- All financial amounts: `DecimalField(max_digits=10, decimal_places=2)` — NEVER use FloatField.
- Visit.pricing_snapshot (JSONField) is immutable after creation.

## 4. API & Security Standards
- Treat Agency endpoints with strict multi-tenancy. A user with `IsAgencyAdmin` can ONLY interact with queries scoped to `agency_id == request.user.agency_id`.
- The SuperAdmin dashboard is separate from the Agency SaaS dashboard. Do not mix their permissions.
- Log critical MoH compliance events (KYC uploads, dispatch completions).
- Visit status changes ONLY via `transition_to()` — follow `ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS` map.

## 5. Development Roadmap (WBS — 9 Phases)
Follow the phases **sequentially**. Every phase has 5 tickets (4 feature + 1 mandatory QA).
See `docs/AGILE_BACKLOG_WBS.md` for full details.

| Phase | Name | Status |
|:---:|:---|:---|
| 1 | Database Refactoring & Multi-Tenancy | ~80% Done |
| 2 | Agency KYC & Onboarding | Not Started |
| 3 | Geospatial Infrastructure | Partial |
| 4 | Two-Tier Dispatch Engine | Partial |
| 5 | Real-Time Sockets | Partial |
| 6 | Financial Escrow & Settlement | Partial |
| 7 | Next.js PWAs (Patient & Nurse) | Skeleton Only |
| 8 | Blackbox System & Disputes | Not Started |
| 9 | AI Copilot & CI/CD | Not Started |

## 6. Development Workflow (Hyper-Pair Programming)
- When generating code, provide the **complete file** if requested, but prefer targeted `diffs` to avoid overwriting unrelated logic.
- Do not remove existing Egyptian Arabic translations. Wateen is an Arabic-first application.
- If you encounter a 500 Error during Next.js SSR, check for missing `'use client'` directives.
- **Always read `AGENTS.md` before starting any task.**

